# Captured Mercado Livre wire bodies (#1087). These are ARTEFACTS, not source:
# `promote:fixtures` writes them with `JSON.stringify(v, null, 2)` and regenerates
# SHAPES.txt from exactly those bytes. Letting prettier reformat them makes the
# generator and the formatter fight — every promote produces a diff and every
# commit normalises it back — which destroys the one property the corpus needs:
# re-promoting an unchanged capture must produce no diff at all.
apps/mercado-livre/lib/marketplace/fixtures/__wire__/

# The Loja Integrada spec leaf inventory is GENERATED (`li-doc.mjs folhas`, one
# leaf per line): the generator owns those bytes, so a regeneration diffs leaf by
# leaf instead of fighting the formatter.
apps/loja-integrada/lib/lojaIntegrada/testing/especificacaoFolhas.json

# Sanitized Loja Integrada fixtures: `sanitizar` writes them with
# `JSON.stringify(v, null, 2)`, and a re-run over an unchanged capture must write
# identical bytes (the Mercado Livre corpus above, same reason).
